  "details": "   * SECURITY UPDATE: Buffer Over-read because of invalid cursor position\n     after \"0;\" range\n     - debian/patches/CVE-2022-1927.patch: check the cursor position when\n       it was set by \";\" in the range\n     - CVE-2022-1927\n   * SECURITY UPDATE: Use After Free in spell command\n     - debian/patches/CVE-2022-2042.patch: initialize \"attr\", check for\n       empty line early\n     - CVE-2022-2042\n   * SECURITY UPDATE: Out-of-bounds Read when regex pattern starts with\n     illegal byte\n     - debian/patches/CVE-2022-2581.patch: do not match a character with an\n       illegal byte\n     - CVE-2022-2581\n   * SECURITY UPDATE: Heap-based Buffer Overflow with for loop over NULL\n     string\n     - debian/patches/CVE-2022-2849.patch: make sure mb_ptr2len()\n       consistently returns zero for NUL\n     - CVE-2022-2849",
